      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I understand the original test. I'll improve understandability by:\n1. Removing the unused `tagSetNamespaceCount` helper method (dead code adds cognitive noise)\n2. Simplifying the fragmented string concatenation in `assertEquals` into a single readable literal\n3. Adding a brief comment to clarify the test intentNow I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removing the unused `tagSetNamespaceCount` reflection helper (dead code that added noise), simplifying the fragmented string concatenation `\"<custom>\\n\" + \"\\n\" + \"Foo\\n\" + \" Bar\" + \"</custom>\"` into a single readable literal `\"<custom>\\n\\nFoo\\n Bar</custom>\"`, and adding a brief comment to clarify the test's setup intent — all while preserving identical runtime behaviour."
